o make this an initializer for the declaration?"],["d33c8370_eb6dfaf8",42,-3,1,"Doesn't this match the default constructor for the AtomicString?"],["df06cbed_29aca87b",42,-3,1,"Use initializer list."],["f2d3e631_dd3f9109",42,-3,1,"Use initializer list."],["f96efe50_40a8ec63",49,-3,1,"Stray semi-colon."],["34a438e9_e1cc6496",43,0,1,"It would only be a problem if the test didn't pass, right? How about: ``` // Since actual and expected values are generated randomly, `assert_equals()` // does not generate deterministic test failure…"],["a2e5fc15_66ea7006",43,0,1,"I'd expect `assert_*` functions to be in testharness.js's namespace. Rename `assert_random_equals` to `test_random_equals`, and use `assert_true(actual === expected, message);` here instead."],["f4651aab_d370df88",43,0,1,"\"should be\""]],0,261],[7197982,20417,289,4.911,3.884,[[0,0.867,213,251],[1,0.133,160,38]],[["44ad6838_1e06e101",49,0,0,"Is that true for many lengths, for instance? Many properties only accept positive lengths. In that case the percentages are known to be positive. Does the spec say if they should be simplified at…"],["51b074c8_4058af57",49,0,1,"more of a question to both Munira and Rune (since the same pattern is used in sibling-* as I see) - we have a bunch of places still that create length resolver with element being nullptr, maybe at…"],["5546635e_426baab9",50,0,0,"wondering, why do we need it now? other functions such as EvaluateTrigonometricFunction seem to be wokring without PLATFORM_EXPORT?"],["63c6a019_cccba87a",49,0,1,"nit: g_empty_atom?"],["695dac4c_ab743396",10,0,1,"\"the random()\""],["71e2e7a6_7856d57e",10,0,1,"\"the random\""],["9cde6b6e_82285cae",51,0,0,"nit: why this comment?"],["a9437ff6_65a36172",10,0,1,"remove"],["e5b2fcb5_a5e2e213",10,0,1,"\"a workaround\""],["efc8e58a_bbad33e8",10,0,1,"Simply 'compute' or 'compute computed'?"],["f075c1c0_dcede10c",49,0,1,"nit: ParseMathFunction has the same code already, maybe extract it to CreateRandomFunction(), so that there is only one place to maintain and then just call it from here and there?"]],0,262],[7213578,20425,405,4.911,3.884,[[0,0.645,214,261],[1,0.336,161,137],[4,0.019,2,7]],[["e6ca3106_89f4208c",52,-2,0,"Is there a proposal to add CSSMathRandom to typed OM? We have shipped multiple calc()-like functions where we have ended up falling back to reifying as a CSSStyleValue instead of doing the work of…"],["232dc45d_580e4cf5",53,-1,1,"css_math_random"],["237eda12_274fe191",53,-1,1,"CSSNumericValueType?"]],0,263],[7236346,20430,37,0.974,0.711,[[0,0.878,215,33],[1,0.122,162,4]],[["446c19c4_acfdf00c",54,0,1,"This 'break' is just temporary to avoid the crash? If so, add a TODO? I don't quite understand what's going on here. When can value be nullptr?"],["a7f3b7f6_9778e52d",55,0,1,"Is it supposed to work eventually? Could we check the expected result of the style set?"]],0,264],[7251111,20433,23,0.518,0.377,[[1,163]],[],0,265],[7218288,20437,305,4.911,3.884,[[0,0.757,216,229],[1,0.243,164,76]],[["45e86d40_be852135",56,-12,0,"I suspect create a new parser context for every longhand will affect parser performance. Could you try run the style perf tests…"],["4e750f56_85d8d0d2",56,-5,1,"This only works for top level math functions. What's the plan to support values like: `background-image: image-set(linear-gradient(black, rgb(0 0 random(...))) 1x)`?"],["e9f66310_42d173e9",49,-5,1,"What about registered custom properties? Should this be CSSPropertyName instead?"],["f12f00b8_1098fda8",56,-5,1,"Could this be handled through the construction instead of exposing the new method?"],["2bd9e352_4a71aebd",42,-3,1,"name?"],["2ed3886b_7cf5befe",49,-3,0,"Is PropertyInfo more than property name? If not, name it CopyWithPropertyNameIfNeeded?"],["32430078_3ac73da9",44,-3,1,"You should pass CSSPropertyName as a const reference to avoid unnecessary copying."],["3c23be12_36cfcd19",57,-3,0,"...WithPropertyName...?"],["8b26dad4_20cb86aa",49,-3,0,"Should this now be called WithPropertyName?"],["b5e29ef9_02e4f722",58,-3,0,"WithPropertyNameIf (everywhere)"]],0,266],[7246178,20437,63,0.974,0.711,[[0,0.548,217,32],[1,0.452,165,31]],[["0b258ae7_b6ced1c5",49,-4,0,"What exactly does element-shared mean, and why don't we need to mark it ReferencedRandom() for MPC in that case? Does it mean it's the same value for every element?"],["3723cfd8_32acd461",59,-4,1,"This isn't entirely true since you skip marking for certain random modes. Add documentation about the exceptions? Or even rename appropriately?"],["b79e9798_0b1577d8",60,-4,1,"\"to\" (I see that you copied from ReferenceSibling(); could you fix that one as well?)"],["2d607e2a_e38c4912",59,-3,1,"Dependent"],["4d58f748_c0e1b3fe",60,-3,1,"ReferenceElementDependentRandom()"],["c090a753_5facc109",60,-3,1,"\"element-dependent random()\"?"],["d41ba73c_336cf18d",61,-3,1,"kElementDependentRandom"]],0,267],[7241411,20440,417,4.911,3.884,[[0,0.888,218,374],[1,0.112,166,45]],[["9aa6a509_24d44d6f",42,-7,1,"Please fix this WARNING reported by ClangTidy: check: google-explicit-constructor single-argument constructors must be marked ... check: google-explicit-constructor single-argument constructors must…"],["b166196e_38a25dfa",43,-7,1,"Could you split out this test change in a separate CL? Then wpt downstream engines have a rationale in the commit message why you did this change."],["f249d563_a5e7e684",45,-7,1,"This looks like a leak to me, in combination with an ever-growing RandomValueCache. If you create 1000 elements which all have a random() value cached based on a key that includes Element, and remove…"],["10d73a91_515adb11",62,-2,1,"Move it down to the valid cases if it's valid."],["5ccd4c88_6c9a813b",49,-2,1,"This needs documentation to say what's going on here. Why you need it."],["cdd4b72b_6e68c844",42,-2,1,"Should the Auto() value be a singleton object?"],["e473197c_b8057124",42,-2,1,"What does it mean that something that is ElementShared becomes IdentElementShared without an ident?"],["f0371539_91d748f7",48,-2,1,"If this is always non-null, I'd pass a const reference instead."],["fc040f95_f2079c48",42,-2,1,"It's not easy to understand that this is also for property-shared random values. Documentation + a better name for this struct."]],0,268],[7277056,20441,35,0.974,0.711,[[1,0.622,167,22],[0,0.378,219,13]],[["5a7015c3_506068fd",43,0,1,"`let i = 0` seems more civilized?"],["63d15dab_67b82cd3",63,0,1,"Shouldn't we return `this` if `random_values_cnt==0`?"],["d1c7fdd8_09c10039",63,0,1,"Don't we want to compare by address here?"]],0,269]]}